1
00:00:58,117 --> 00:01:05,127
<v Tutor>Jerry, how did it go with preparing your lessons? Is there anything you would like to discuss?


2
00:01:05,127 --> 00:01:10,936
<v Jerry>Well, this is actually the first time that I have ever taught in an elementary classroom. 


3
00:01:10,936 --> 00:01:19,860
<v Jerry>After 8 years of learning pedagogy, I want to practice what I’ve learned in an instructive manner, but I’m a bit stuck right now. 


4
00:01:19,860 --> 00:01:23,910
<v Jerry>You know the topic 1 want them to research is a bit hard for pupils.

5
00:01:23,910 --> 00:01:27,710
 <v Jerry>I’m afraid that they won’t be able to handle it on their own. 

6
00:01:27,710 --> 00:01:32,799
<v Jerry>So I need new ideas on designing more effective teaching methods. 

7
00:01:32,799 --> 00:01:36,336
<v Jerry>Mr.Carter, do you have any suggestions?

8
00:01:36,336 --> 00:01:43,785
<v Tutor>Well, you should probably read this book called Professional Learning, written by J.K. Simmons. 


9
00:01:43,785 --> 00:01:52,910
<v Tutor>He is a professor who just transferred here last semester but is already popular amongst the students for his creative teaching methods. 


10
00:01:52,910 --> 00:02:01,539
<v Tutor>There is an extensive range of learning approaches mentioned in the book including approaches for team research, which might be helpful to you.

11
00:02:01,529 --> 00:02:05,691
<v Jerry>You mean dividing the students into groups to do research? 


12
00:02:05,691 --> 00:02:09,541
<v Jerry>I’ve never thought of this before. How does it work?

13
00:02:09,541 --> 00:02:15,058
<v Tutor>Professor Simmons has already demonstrated how efficient this approach can be.
 

14
00:02:15,058 --> 00:02:24,117
<v Tutor>Basically it aims to increase cooperation between students so they can present the results in a collaborative fashion. 

15
00:02:24,117 --> 00:02:28,730
<v Tutor>It helps them to develop their own voice and perspective.


16
00:02:28,730 --> 00:02:31,470
<v Jerry>I’ll check out the book as soon as possible. 


17
00:02:31,470 --> 00:02:37,320
<v Jerry>It seems I can borrow some of the essential concepts and work them into my course design.

18
00:03:13,642 --> 00:03:22,423
<v Jerry>Well, I was thinking maybe I could use both observation and nonobservation as part of my teaching methodology. 

19
00:03:22,423 --> 00:03:25,008
<v Jerry>Could you take a look at my teaching plan?


20
00:03:25,008 --> 00:03:30,047
<v Tutor>Sure. What kind of observational methods do you have in mind?


21
00:03:30,047 --> 00:03:34,624
<v Jerry>For the observational part, I intend to include two approaches. 


22
00:03:34,624 --> 00:03:38,305
<v Jerry>First, the pupils can assess each other’s behaviour. 

23
00:03:38,305 --> 00:03:45,778
<v Jerry>I feel that reviewing fellow students through criteria-based reference evaluation allows constructive feedback. 

24
00:03:45,778 --> 00:03:50,369
<v Jerry>It can also improve their understanding of the subject material.

25
00:03:50,369 --> 00:03:56,274
<v Tutor>That’s a smart move for a large class that would be hard to observe all by yourself.


26
00:03:56,274 --> 00:04:02,901
 <v Tutor>Also, you might want to get the feedback from several different individuals rather than just one. 

27
00:04:02,901 --> 00:04:06,210
<v Tutor>So how do you plan to carry out the peer assessments?

28
00:04:06,200 --> 00:04:16,043
<v Jerry>Oh, every pupil will be required to write a diary, which includes group projects, presentations and in-class discussions. 

29
00:04:16,043 --> 00:04:25,231
<v Jerry>They’ll put down their remarks. I’ll collect them on a regular basis which can also help me see whether they can keep up or not.

30
00:04:25,231 --> 00:04:27,932
<v Tutor>Good, what else do you intend to do?


31
00:04:27,932 --> 00:04:31,809
<v Jerry>Besides that, I also plan to do video recording. 


32
00:04:31,809 --> 00:04:37,075
<v Jerry>I’ve already purchased a camera just in case I miss anything important. 

33
00:04:37,075 --> 00:04:41,771
<v Jerry>I can go back and review their performances anytime I want.


34
00:04:41,771 --> 00:04:44,956
<v Tutor>Would you record every in-class activity?


35
00:04:44,956 --> 00:04:52,310
<v Jerry>No, I’ll just keep track of an in-class simulation, which would require every pupil to fully participate.


36
00:04:52,310 --> 00:05:01,810
 <v Jerry>Students will act as members of a City Council meeting, discussing issues like whether or not prohibition should be instated in the United States.

37
00:05:01,810 --> 00:05:06,328
<v Tutor>This kind of teaching method is both inspiring and challenging. 


38
00:05:06,328 --> 00:05:11,753
<v Tutor>I can’t wait to see how yours work out. Do you send me a copy of the assessment afterwards, will you?


39
00:05:11,753 --> 00:05:12,899
<v Jerry>No problem.


40
00:05:12,899 --> 00:05:18,006
<v Tutor>So what do you have in mind for the non-observational approaches?


41
00:05:18,006 --> 00:05:23,693
<v Jerry>Well, my plan is to quantify the statistics. Numbers do not lie.


42
00:05:23,693 --> 00:05:29,211
 <v Jerry>It is the most direct way to measure their performance. See how well they’ve learned.

43
00:05:29,211 --> 00:05:30,756
<v Tutor>Where does the data come from?


44
00:05:30,756 --> 00:05:41,372
<v Jerry>I’ll evaluate the test results including the mid-term, final exam and pop quizzes, which would only take up about 40 percent of the overall assessment.


45
00:05:41,372 --> 00:05:47,166
<v Tutor>Sounds like a lot of tests and assignments. Please remember that you don’t want to wear out your students. 


46
00:05:47,166 --> 00:05:54,462
<v Tutor>Keeping them engaged is the key to efficient learning. Once they are exhausted, they just stop trying.

47
00:05:54,462 --> 00:05:58,629
<v Jerry>Oh, I haven’t thought about that. You are right. 


48
00:05:58,629 --> 00:06:06,498
<v Jerry>I don’t want to frighten them with tons of assignments and exams. I’ll make note of that. Thanks for the advice.

49
00:06:06,498 --> 00:06:09,822
<v Tutor>I remember last time you mentioned questionnaires, right?


50
00:06:09,822 --> 00:06:13,640
<v Jerry>That’s true. But it is not for my students. 

51
00:06:13,640 --> 00:06:21,031
<v Jerry>In fact, they have to design their own questionnaires and choose the respondents using the Internet. 


52
00:06:21,031 --> 00:06:27,056
<v Jerry>As a complement of other teaching activities, it would deepen the creative learning process.


53
00:06:27,056 --> 00:06:28,515
<v Tutor>Is that all?


54
00:06:28,515 --> 00:06:32,308
<v Jerry>Oh, the pupils will have to conduct interviews of their own. 


55
00:06:32,308 --> 00:06:40,867
<v Jerry>And for this, they get to choose anyone they like, including relatives, friends and acquaintances to answer the questions.

56
00:06:40,867 --> 00:06:47,841
<v Tutor>Seems to me that you have figured out most of your teaching methods. But you still need to polish some of the activities...